[
  {
    "sha": "1beb1b027c20ad7740888b625c0e89e48aa7e8a2",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDFiZWIxYjAyN2MyMGFkNzc0MDg4OGI2MjVjMGU4OWU0OGFhN2U4YTI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T18:09:44Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T18:09:44Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim,app): a vertical rapid down into uncut stock is a rapid in stock\n\nVerify's rapid law (d) skipped every vertical rapid as a retract up the\ntool's own kerf, so a rapid going DOWN into declared stock posted\nsilently. A downward vertical rapid whose end is below the surface the\ncuts before it left at its column, inside the stock, is now\nRapidInStock; a peck or a later level's re-entry down its own earlier\nplunge stays clean (cut order), and so does a retract up.\n\nThe turned family's Envelope kinds stand the spindle axis on world Z,\nso their axial rapids read as column dives the column cannot judge (it\ncannot see the meridian). operation/turning_rapids drops the column\nlaw's verdict on a turned path's axial rapids only, so that family\nreads exactly as before.\n\nFixtures that rapided into their own declared stock now declare stock\nto their top: posting's contour_and_drill and Deep1, control_comp and\noperations' shell switch (blocks 10/20 mm over a top-5 op), and\npocket3d_hsm's verify context (stock top 0 over a top -5 op). No golden\nchanged. Triage table in RECOMMENDED.md.\n\nFixes #96\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
