      "message": "fix(sim,app): the vertical-rapid law reads what earlier ops cut\n\nReview fixes for PR #105:\n\n- The column law read only this op's own cuts and the raw stock top,\n  so face-then-contour and pocket-then-drill programs that post today\n  were refused. collect_job now gathers a rest::PriorPlan (stock grid +\n  the cached moves of every cutting op ahead in the setup) for every\n  untilted, non-turned op; run_job simulates it only when verify has\n  convicted a rapid, and verify::acquit_by_prior keeps a vertical\n  dive's conviction only while it also ends below the prior surface\n  (highest column under the tool disc; an unknown prior is raw stock).\n- pocket3d_hsm: the op's top_z is raised to 0, the stock its load\n  reader declares, and the verify stock top is back at 0 (levels and\n  pinned numbers unchanged).\n- verify's module doc states the vertical-dive law.\n- turning_rapids unit test: only the axial conviction is dropped.\n\nRefs #96\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
